      "card_ids": ["C06","C11","C19","C29","C09","C01","C03","C12","C14","C02","C04","C16","C13"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L5 Caco-2 permeability records for polar glycosides and aminoglycosides show low absorptive permeability: paromomycin negligible (C58), breviscapine 4.78×10^-7 cm/s (C66), baicalin 0.01-0.02×10^-6 cm/s (C56), quercetin 3-O-glucuronide 0.11×10^-6 cm/s (C61), acteoside 0.24-0.34×10^-6 cm/s (C57, C62), echinacoside 0.76×10^-6 cm/s (C55), morroniside 0.55-0.62×10^-6 cm/s (C60), and PGA5 lower than mannitol (C59).",
      "card_ids": ["C55","C56","C57","C58","C59","C60","C61","C62","C66"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "The single higher in vitro value, tobramycin sulphate control Papp 1.78×10^-6 cm/s (C64), is not an oral bioavailability measurement and does not establish F≥20% for the query.",
      "card_ids": ["C64"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "The query's extreme polarity, full ionization, and very low estimated logD are consistent with the low-permeability profile of these analogs; no affirmative threshold-relevant evidence supports F≥20%.",
      "card_ids": ["C06","C01","C14","C58","C66"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L6 hepatic clearance/metabolic stability records concern unrelated glucuronides, acyl glucuronides, and FMO substrates (C67-C78) and provide no query-specific hepatic clearance or metabolic stability data; they do not alter the low prediction.",
      "card_ids": ["C67","C68","C69","C70","C71","C72","C73","C74","C75","C76","C77","C78"]
    }
  ],
  "new_evidence_assessment": [
    {
      "family": "hepatic_clearance_metabolic_stability",
      "applicability": "low",
      "direction": "neutral_or_unclear",
      "decision_effect": "no_change",
      "card_ids": ["C67","C68","C69","C70","C71","C72","C73","C74","C75","C76","C77","C78"]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct oral bioavailability measurement exists for the exact query disaccharide.",
    "L6 hepatic clearance/metabolic stability records are for unrelated glucuronides, acyl glucuronides, and FMO substrates and provide no query-specific hepatic extraction or metabolic stability data.",
    "No query-specific intestinal permeability, efflux, or active transport data are available.",
    "No data on possible active uptake or transporter involvement for the exact molecule.",
    "C64 is a single in vitro permeability value without an F measurement and does not resolve threshold-relevant absorption."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "The query is an extremely polar, fully ionized sulfated disaccharide. Direct human F values for closely related sulfated/polar molecules are all below 20%, and L5 Caco-2 permeability data for polar glycosides and aminoglycosides reinforce a severe absorption barrier. L6 hepatic clearance/metabolic stability records are not query-specific and do not change the assessment. The low prediction is retained with high confidence."
}

